  m_text: Jean-Michel Basquiat was a self-taught, influential African American artist
    who rose to fame in the 1980s New York art scene. His work, which blended graffiti
    and Abstract Expressionism, challenged traditional boundaries and conveyed powerful
    messages about race, politics, and society. Basquiat first gained attention in
    the late 1970s for his cryptic graffiti under the name "SAMO".
