  m_text: Andy Warhol was a leading figure in the 1960s Pop Art movement and is considered
    one of the most influential artists of the 20th century. Warhol was a successful
    commercial illustrator for magazines and ads before transitioning to fine art.
    His work blurred the lines between mainstream and fine art, and he's known for
    his silkscreen paintings of celebrities like Marilyn Monroe and Jackie Kennedy,
    as well as his depictions of everyday objects like Campbell's soup cans.
