  m_text: Keith Allen Haring was an American artist and activist who emerged from
    the 1980s New York City graffiti scene. His work combined street art and fine
    art, and his use of bright colors and thick black lines became his signature
    style. Haring's art often featured cartoon-like characters like barking dogs
    and crawling babies, and responded to social and political issues. He created
    hundreds of chalk drawings in the New York subway and on public poster marquees.
