  m_text: "Salvador Domingo Felipe Jacinto Dal\xED i Dom\xE8nech was a Spanish artist
    and filmmaker who is considered a leader of the Surrealist movement and one of
    the most influential artists of the 20th century. His technically precise and
    unusual paintings, sculptures, and films explored subconscious imagery, dreams,
    sexuality, religion, and science. His 1931 painting The Persistence of Memory,
    depicting melting watches, is arguably his most famous work. \n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
