      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Gustav Klimt was an Austrian painter and a leader of the Vienna Secession
    movement. He's known for his opulent, Byzantine-inspired portraits of women,
    often featuring gold and eroticism. Klimt's work was a radical departure from
    artistic convention, and he's considered a pioneer of Austrian Modernism. In
    1897, Klimt and other artists broke away from the conservative K\xFCnstlerhaus
    to form the Vienna Secession, a group that embraced the international avant garde."
