  m_text: Georges Pierre Seurat was a French Post-Impressionist artist who invented
    the painting technique known as pointillism. Pointillism involves applying many
    small dots of pure color to a canvas, which blend together from a distance to
    form an image. Seurat believed that juxtaposing tiny dabs of color created more
    intense and luminous hues through optical blending.
