  m_text: Edgar Degas was a French Impressionist artist who focused on modern life
    and human figures in everyday situations. He's best known for his paintings of
    ballet dancers, often backstage, capturing their grace and power. His work is
    known for its energy and focus on people, and he invented new techniques to depict
    movement. Degas also created portraits, history paintings, and sculptures, and
    worked in pastels, printmaking, and bronze.
