  m_text: 'Marc Chagall was a Russian-French artist and a leader of modern art. His
    dreamlike style, inspired by Russian folktales and Jewish stories, incorporated
    bright colors, exaggerated proportions, and overlapping images. His work drew
    from cubism, expressionism, and fauvism, but defied categorization. Chagall worked
    in many mediums, including paintings, etchings, stained glass, ceramics, tapestries,
    and set designs for theater and ballet. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
