  m_text: 'Pieter Cornelis Mondriaan was a Dutch painter and art theorist who played
    a key role in the development of abstract art. He''s known for his geometric
    paintings using black lines and rectangles of red, yellow, and blue. His abstract
    style, which he called Neo-Plasticism, was influenced by Cubism and aimed to
    represent modern reality through the interaction of colors and forms on the canvas. '
