  m_text: Vincent Willem van Gogh was a Dutch Post-Impressionist painter who created
    around 2,100 artworks in just over a decade. His work, known for its vivid colors
    and expressive brushwork, is considered highly influential in Western art and
    Expressionism. Van Gogh's early paintings depicted nature and peasants in earthy
    tones, but he was later influenced by Impressionism and Japanese prints.
